A column flex container with a preferred aspect ratio now grows to the
sum of its items’ outer hypothetical main sizes, as Blink’s
FlexLayoutAlgorithm does: Its intrinsic block size for a column
container is the sum of the items’ hypothetical main sizes, and that’s
the automatic minimum for a box with an aspect ratio.

Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 (the build
Playwright ships), the test’s seventeen cases give the container and
each of its items the same heights in all three engines, and the same
as Ladybird does now: flexible and scrollable items, two items, gaps,
min-height: 0 on an item or the container, max-height, overflow:
hidden, contain: size, or contain: inline-size on the container,
wrapping, column-reverse, a row container, and cards that are flex
items or absolutely positioned.
